# fixedbugs, defect 324, lane b10-cli, 2026-10-04.
#
# Zeros before a base's marker, `00x7`: the prefix's one zero written more
# than once. `leading_zero` advised `0o0` for the zeros, which runs into the
# `x` after them as a digit no octal number has. The advice is now one zero,
# `0x7` once applied. The letters after the zeros are still told a second
# time, `expected_end_of_line`, as they were; the advice is
# `selfhost/number.hero`'s test of defect 324.
#
# 2026-10-05, defect 329, lane b11-misc: the letters are told once. What
# joins the zeros is the refused literal's, said in its note, so the second
# message, `expected_end_of_line`, is gone from this line.

function main()
    a = 00x7    #~ leading_zero
    print(a)
